 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Roughly repeat back what you've heard, so you build confidence that you' following the conversation. Or you could pretend with toys, like a pretend phone call. Roughly whisper, and stop if someone looks upset. The key is to be self aware of how loud you are. You could also practice with recorded lessons, but a toy phone call with a friend as the listener is the most immersive. Lots of people do. Start with simple phrases and build up, and remember that everyone sounds silly at first. Yes, even me. Sure, try Hello, how are you, in Italian. It' Ciao, come stai?",
